{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-206803-r4517767","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Struffoli (Neapolitan Honey Fried Dough)","sourcePageId":206803,"sourceRevision":"4517767","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T03:03:44Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Struffoli%20(Neapolitan%20Honey%20Fried%20Dough)&oldid=4517767","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:52.726Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Italian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for fritters","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using cream of tartar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using orange","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"98bc01f2e88876535ee341434f68215cc0ebad98c198e0be324f05a769e5b406","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Fritter recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Italy]]\n\n'''Struffoli''' is a fried Neapolitan [[Cookbook:Dessert|dessert]].\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Dough ===\n\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ½ cup dry [[Cookbook:Sherry|sherry]]\n* [[Cookbook:Flour|Flour]]\n* [[Cookbook:Shortening|Shortening]] or oil for deep frying\n\n===Glaze===\n\n* 1½ cups white granulated sugar\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Orange|orange]] zest\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Combine eggs, oil, baking powder, cream of tartar, sugar, and sherry. Mix in enough flour to make a [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]]. The dough should be somewhat sticky but still workable.\n# Shape dough into small balls, about ½ inch in diameter.\n# Heat the shortening or oil to 350–375°F. [[Cookbook:Deep fry|Deep fry]] the dough balls until golden brown and cooked through.\n# Mix all the glaze ingredients over low heat until sugar is dissolved. Dip each fritter into the glaze, and remove.\n\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fritters]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n\n[[it:Libro di cucina/Ricette/Struffoli]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Struffoli (Neapolitan Honey Fried Dough)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 eggs","sourceText":"6 eggs","amountText":"6 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"6 tbsp vegetable oil","sourceText":"6 tbsp vegetable oil","amountText":"6 tbsp vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBindi